You are an expert developer. We are verifying the code generated by LLM to fix the SonarQube warning titled " "wait(...)" should be used instead of "Thread.sleep(...)" when a lock is held " which has the following description:
If `Thread.sleep(...)` is called when the current thread holds a lock, it could lead to performance and scalability issues, or even worse to deadlocks because the execution of the thread holding the lock is frozen. It’s better to call `wait(...)` on the monitor object to temporarily release the lock and allow other threads to run.

Noncompliant Code Example
    
    
    public void doSomething(){
      synchronized(monitor) {
        while(notReady()){
          Thread.sleep(200);
        }
        process();
      }
      ...
    }
    

Compliant Solution
    
    
    public void doSomething(){
      synchronized(monitor) {
        while(notReady()){
          monitor.wait(200);
        }
        process();
      }
      ...
    }
    

See

  * [CERT, LCK09-J.](https://wiki.sei.cmu.edu/confluence/x/YTdGBQ) \- Do not perform operations that can block while holding a lock

 

